\section{S7 Core Class Architecture}{

All model objects are organized under an explicit, compositional S7 class
hierarchy:
\describe{
\item{\code{MVBU_CategoryRepresentation}}{Abstract base class for individual
category representations, encapsulating category parameters, cue
labels, and likelihood functions.}
\item{\code{MVBU_CategoryRepresentationTemplate}}{Validated collection of
category representations forming a perceptual inventory or template.}
\item{\code{MVBU_CognitiveModel}}{Decision model pairing a category template
with decision behavior (decision rule, category priors, lapse rate,
lapse bias, and perceptual noise).}
\item{\code{MVBU_IdealObserver}}{Subclass of \code{MVBU_CognitiveModel} for
observers with fixed generative category distributions.}
\item{\code{MVBU_IdealAdaptor}}{Subclass of \code{MVBU_CognitiveModel} for adaptors
with conjugate prior beliefs that update incrementally from exposure.}
\item{\code{MVBU_Stanfit}}{Wrapper for \code{rstan} \code{stanfit} objects inferring
prior beliefs, lapse parameters, and noise from behavioral test data.}
\item{\code{MVBU_StanfitInput}}{Container for exposure data, test data,
priors, and transformation functions used to prepare Stan inputs.}
\item{\code{MVBU_Staninput}}{Validated input data list passed to Stan models.}
}
}

\section{Supported Model Families}{

\code{MVBeliefUpdatr} provides concrete S7 classes and constructors across seven
families:
\describe{
\item{\code{UVG} / \code{NIX}}{Univariate Gaussian ideal observers
(\link{UVG_IdealObserver}) and Normal-Inverse-Chisquare ideal adaptors
(\link{NIX_IdealAdaptor}).}
\item{\code{MUVG} / \code{MNIX}}{Multi-univariate Gaussian ideal observers
(\link{MUVG_IdealObserver}) and independent Normal-Inverse-Chisquare cue
integration adaptors (\link{MNIX_IdealAdaptor}).}
\item{\code{MVG} / \code{NIW}}{Multivariate Gaussian ideal observers
(\link{MVG_IdealObserver}) and Normal-Inverse-Wishart ideal adaptors
(\link{NIW_IdealAdaptor}).}
\item{\code{EXEMPLAR}}{Exemplar-based categorization models (\link{Exemplar_Model})
with kernel density estimation over stored exemplars.}
}
}

